text:
Q: Flowing ideas across a page A: <p>The overlap happens because your current setup only staggers bubbles by <em>lane</em> and <em>initial x-offset</em> — it never stops a faster bubble from catching up to a slower one ahead of it in the same lane, and when a bubble exits and respawns, it always jumps back to the same fixed <code>areaWidth + reentryOffset</code>, regardless of whether another bubble is already sitting right there. Lanes alone don't guarantee spacing over time.</p>
<p>The fix is to treat each lane like a single-file conveyor belt: keep bubbles in a fixed front-to-back order, and each frame clamp a bubble's position so it can never get closer than a minimum gap to the bubble ahead of it. When a bubble exits on the left, it respawns <em>behind the last bubble in its own lane</em> (not at a fixed offset), so it can never spawn on top of something already there.</p>
<p>New version vs. your original <code>initOpinionFlow</code>:</p>
<ol>
<li><p><strong>Bubbles are grouped into per-lane queues</strong>, in a fixed front-to-back order (based on their original index). That order never changes — a bubble can never pass the one ahead of it in its lane.</p>
</li>
<li><p><strong>Every frame, each bubble is clamped</strong> so it can't get closer than <code>GAP</code> (22px) to the bubble ahead of it in the same lane: <code>bubble.x = Math.max(bubble.x, ahead.x + ahead.width + GAP)</code>. This is what actually stops the overlap — previously nothing prevented a faster bubble from sliding under/behind a slower one.</p>
</li>
<li><p><strong>Respawn is queue-aware.</strong> When the front bubble of a lane exits the left edge, it's moved to the back of that lane's queue and placed at <code>lastBubble.x + lastBubble.width + GAP</code> — never at a fixed offset that might already be occupied.</p>
</li>
<li><p>Vertical sine drift is untouched (56px lane spacing comfortably exceeds the max ±7px drift, so lanes don't cross vertically — that wasn't actually your bug).</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p>A couple of tuning knobs worth knowing about:</p>
<ul>
<li><p><strong><code>GAP</code></strong> — increase it if you still see bubbles feeling crowded; decrease for a denser board.</p>
</li>
<li><p>Because slower bubbles set the pace for everything behind them in their lane, a very slow bubble can create a visible &quot;traffic jam&quot; trailing it. If that bothers you visually, either narrow the speed range (<code>0.45 + (index % 4) * 0.07</code> → tighten the spread) or increase <code>laneCount</code> so there are fewer bubbles competing per lane.</p>
<pre class="lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;
&lt;html lang=&quot;en&quot;&gt;
&lt;head&gt;
&lt;meta charset=&quot;UTF-8&quot; /&gt;
&lt;title&gt;Opinion bubbles - fixed&lt;/title&gt;
&lt;style&gt;
  :root {
    --muted: #9aa4b2;
  }
  body {
    background: #0f1115;
    font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, &quot;Segoe UI&quot;, sans-serif;
    padding: 40px;
  }
  .opinions-section {
    margin-top: 18px;
    padding-top: 8px;
    max-width: 720px;
  }
  .opinions-section h3 {
    margin: 0 0 14px;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .opinion-clouds {
    position: relative;
    min-height: 260px;
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
    border-radius: 28px;
    padding: 18px;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.025);
    box-shadow: inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.04);
  }
  .opinion-cloud {
    position: absolute;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    padding: 11px 16px;
    border-radius: 999px;
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.16);
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.06);
    color: #eef2f7;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.2;
    box-shadow: 0 8px 20px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.16);
    backdrop-filter: blur(12px);
    -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(12px);
    white-space: nowrap;
    will-change: left, top;
    max-width: calc(100% - 36px);
    overflow: hidden;
    text-overflow: ellipsis;
  }
  .opinion-cloud::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    inset: 2px;
    border-radius: inherit;
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.05);
    pointer-events: none;
  }
&lt;/style&gt;
&lt;/head&gt;
&lt;body&gt;

&lt;section class=&quot;opinions-section&quot; aria-label=&quot;What people think of Jay&quot;&gt;
  &lt;h3&gt;Opinions&lt;/h3&gt;
  &lt;div class=&quot;opinion-clouds&quot; id=&quot;opinionArea&quot;&gt;
    &lt;span class=&quot;opinion-cloud&quot;&gt;emotionally intelligent&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class=&quot;opinion-cloud&quot;&gt;deeply thoughtful&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class=&quot;opinion-cloud&quot;&gt;makes you feel seen&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class=&quot;opinion-cloud&quot;&gt;comforting to be around&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class=&quot;opinion-cloud&quot;&gt;genuinely kind-hearted&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class=&quot;opinion-cloud&quot;&gt;appreciative&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class=&quot;opinion-cloud&quot;&gt;compassionate&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class=&quot;opinion-cloud&quot;&gt;one of the kindest people I know&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class=&quot;opinion-cloud&quot;&gt;effortlessly warm&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class=&quot;opinion-cloud&quot;&gt;has a beautiful way with people&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class=&quot;opinion-cloud&quot;&gt;so easy to talk to&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class=&quot;opinion-cloud&quot;&gt;makes kindness feel natural&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class=&quot;opinion-cloud&quot;&gt;makes you feel safe&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class=&quot;opinion-cloud&quot;&gt;unbelievably sincere&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/section&gt;

&lt;script&gt;
  const opinionArea = document.getElementById('opinionArea');
  const opinionClouds = Array.from(opinionArea.querySelectorAll('.opinion-cloud'));
  let animationFrameId = null;

  const GAP = 22; // min horizontal gap enforced between two bubbles in the same lane

  function initOpinionFlow() {
    if (animationFrameId) cancelAnimationFrame(animationFrameId);

    const areaWidth = opinionArea.clientWidth;
    const areaHeight = opinionArea.clientHeight;
    const laneGap = 56;
    const laneCount = Math.max(
      3,
      Math.min(5, Math.floor((areaHeight - 24) / laneGap) + 1)
    );
    const lanes = Array.from({ length: laneCount }, (_, i) =&gt; 20 + i * laneGap);

    const bubbles = opinionClouds.map((cloud, index) =&gt; ({
      el: cloud,
      lane: index % laneCount,
      x: 0,
      y: lanes[index % laneCount],
      speed: 0.45 + (index % 4) * 0.07,
      drift: 3 + (index % 3) * 2,
      phase: index * 0.95,
      width: cloud.offsetWidth,
      height: cloud.offsetHeight,
    }));

    // group bubbles by lane, preserving index order -&gt; this order becomes
    // the fixed front-to-back queue order for that lane
    const laneQueues = Array.from({ length: laneCount }, () =&gt; []);
    bubbles.forEach((b) =&gt; laneQueues[b.lane].push(b));

    // spread bubbles out along each lane initially so nothing spawns stacked
    laneQueues.forEach((queue) =&gt; {
      let x = areaWidth + 40;
      queue.forEach((b) =&gt; {
        b.x = x;
        x += b.width + GAP + Math.random() * 40;
      });
    });

    function respawnAtBack(bubble, queue) {
      const last = queue[queue.length - 1];
      const backX = last ? last.x + last.width + GAP : areaWidth + 40;
      bubble.x = Math.max(areaWidth + 40, backX);
    }

    function animate(now) {
      const height = opinionArea.clientHeight;

      laneQueues.forEach((queue) =&gt; {
        let ahead = null;

        queue.forEach((bubble) =&gt; {
          bubble.x -= bubble.speed;

          // never let this bubble get closer than GAP to the one ahead of it
          if (ahead) {
            const minAllowedX = ahead.x + ahead.width + GAP;
            if (bubble.x &lt; minAllowedX) bubble.x = minAllowedX;
          }

          bubble.y =
            lanes[bubble.lane] +
            Math.sin(now * 0.0012 + bubble.phase) * bubble.drift;
          bubble.y = Math.max(
            10,
            Math.min(height - bubble.height - 10, bubble.y)
          );

          bubble.el.style.left = `${bubble.x}px`;
          bubble.el.style.top = `${bubble.y}px`;

          ahead = bubble;
        });

        // the front bubble (queue[0]) is the only one that can ever fully
        // exit on the left, since every bubble behind it is clamped
        const front = queue[0];
        if (front &amp;&amp; front.x &lt; -front.width - 24) {
          queue.shift();
          respawnAtBack(front, queue);
          queue.push(front);
        }
      });

      animationFrameId = requestAnimationFrame(animate);
    }

    animationFrameId = requestAnimationFrame(animate);
  }

  window.addEventListener('load', initOpinionFlow);
  window.addEventListener('resize', initOpinionFlow);
&lt;/script&gt;

&lt;/body&gt;
&lt;/html&gt;

</code></pre>
</li>
</ul>
